## Issues

- [ ] `description` is 249 chars (just over cap 200). Trim to ≤200.
  Traces to: `description` field | Brevity Contract caps
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] `intent` is 249 words (cap 100). Restates description with added
  paragraphs about state membership, no-stat-invariant, name-as-metadata
  rule, store-in-future-name rationale.
  Traces to: `intent` field | Brevity Contract caps
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] `outcomes.desired` has 13 items (cap 4); each is paragraph length.
  Items 5-9 each describe one of the four brain status states by name.
  Items 10-12 enumerate the no-`backend`, no-`rootPath`, no-`invalid-path`
  field rejection rules — restating the closed-vocabulary invariant from
  the parent buildBrainState spec. Compress.
  Traces to: `outcomes.desired` | Brevity Contract caps + Sibling-redundancy + outcomes-purpose test
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Sibling-redundancy

- [ ] `outcomes.undesired` has ~14 paragraph-length items enumerating retired
  regressions (the `backend` field, the `rootPath` field, the `invalid-path`
  state, drift auto-resolution, conflating `no-brain-aide` with `no-mcp-entry`).
  Forbidden content.
  Traces to: `outcomes.undesired` | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Forbidden-content

- [ ] `## Context` is ~400 words (cap ~150). Recapitulates the boot-sequence
  context, the staleness-vs-brain-state split, the passive-reporter
  invariant, the user-owned-config-vs-derived-mcp-json relationship.
  Traces to: `## Context` | Brevity Contract caps + Sibling-redundancy
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Sibling-redundancy

- [ ] `## Strategy` has 9 paragraph-length decisions (cap ~5). Each restates
  one slice of the contract: independent fields, staleness-detection-shape,
  buildBrainState-fully-delegated, four-state vocabulary, `no-brain-aide`-distinct-from-`no-mcp-entry`,
  `mcp-drift`-as-hard-halt, no-`backend` field, no-`rootPath` field,
  no-mutation. Most are restatements of buildBrainState's contract.
  Traces to: `## Strategy` | Brevity Contract caps + Sibling-redundancy
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Sibling-redundancy

- [ ] `## Good examples` and `## Bad examples` reproduce JSON return shapes
  with exact brand strings, exact server version numbers, exact path strings,
  exact store-name strings. Forbidden content (exact strings).
  Traces to: examples sections | Forbidden content
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Forbidden-content

- [ ] Sibling redundancy with `src/service/buildBrainState/.aide`: the
  four-state vocabulary, the no-stat invariant, the no-auto-repair
  contract, the never-throws guarantee, the no-`backend`-field, the
  no-`rootPath`-field — all restated from the buildBrainState sibling.
  This is a forwarder; it should commit to "forwards `buildBrainState`'s
  state union unchanged" and let buildBrainState own the contract.
  Traces to: outcomes, Strategy | Sibling-redundancy doctrine
  Misalignment: spec-gap
  Category: Sibling-redundancy

## Retro

aide_info is one of the best examples in the tree of a forwarder that
restates its delegate's contract. The fix is structural: this spec
commits to "the orchestrator's boot probe; reports staleness via
`.aide/versions.json` comparison; forwards `buildBrainState`'s state
union unchanged" and lets the sibling own the brain-state contract.
~70% of current outcomes vanish under that prune.
